{"title":"Career Roadmap · Cardiac OT Technologist","role":"Cardiac OT Technologist","summary":"A Cardiac OT Technologist is an allied-health professional who supports the multidisciplinary team during cardiac and cardiothoracic surgical procedures.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Anaesthesia Assistant / Perfusion / Cardiac Anaesthesia Tech"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Cardiac OT Technologist is an allied-health professional who supports the multidisciplinary team during cardiac and cardiothoracic surgical procedures."},{"type":"p","text":"The role combines:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cardiac operating-theatre preparation"},{"text":"Surgical equipment readiness"},{"text":"Anaesthesia support"},{"text":"Patient positioning"},{"text":"Surgical consumable preparation"},{"text":"Sterile-field support"},{"text":"Cardiac monitoring equipment setup"},{"text":"Emergency preparedness"},{"text":"Equipment handling"},{"text":"Infection prevention"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Post-procedure theatre turnover"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Cardiac OT Technologists typically work alongside:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cardiothoracic surgeons"},{"text":"Cardiac anaesthesiologists"},{"text":"Perfusionists"},{"text":"Nurses"},{"text":"Cardiac technologists"},{"text":"Other operating-room professionals"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Qualification note","text":"“Cardiac OT Technologist” is a specialized role and terminology varies between institutions. A generic B.Sc/BPT/BOT/BMLT qualification should not automatically be treated as sufficient. Students should pursue a recognized cardiac care/cardiac OT/operation theatre technology or other relevant allied-health qualification with supervised clinical training. A Cardiac OT Technologist supports the surgical team and does not independently perform cardiac surgery, anaesthesia or cardiopulmonary bypass."}]},{"heading":"Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Class 12","Recognized Cardiac / OT Technology Qualification","Clinical Internship","Operation Theatre + Cardiac Surgery Exposure","Junior Cardiac OT Technologist","Cardiac OT Technologist","Senior Cardiac OT Technologist","Cardiac OT Specialist / Coordinator","Cardiothoracic OT Manager / Clinical Educator"]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced pathway"},{"type":"flow","items":["Relevant Allied-Health Qualification","Cardiac OT Clinical Training","Cardiac Surgery Internship","Cardiac OT Technologist","Advanced Cardiac OT Skills","Senior Technologist","OT Coordinator / Clinical Applications Specialist"]}]},{"heading":"What You Learn During UG","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Biomedical Foundation"},{"type":"h","text":"Core subjects"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Anatomy"},{"text":"Physiology"},{"text":"Biochemistry"},{"text":"Microbiology"},{"text":"Pathology"},{"text":"Pharmacology"},{"text":"Nutrition"},{"text":"Basic nursing/patient care"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Cardiac foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Heart anatomy"},{"text":"Cardiac chambers"},{"text":"Valves"},{"text":"Coronary circulation"},{"text":"Cardiac conduction"},{"text":"Blood circulation"},{"text":"Basic ECG concepts"},{"text":"Cardiovascular diseases"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional skills"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient identification"},{"text":"Vital signs"},{"text":"Infection control"},{"text":"Basic life support"},{"text":"Patient communication"},{"text":"Medical terminology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Operation Theatre Technology"},{"type":"p","text":"Students develop fundamental OT competencies."},{"type":"h","text":"OT concepts"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Surgical asepsis"},{"text":"Sterile technique"},{"text":"Surgical instruments"},{"text":"Surgical preparation"},{"text":"Patient positio