are environments increasingly use technologies such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ECMO"},{"text":"Mechanical circulatory support"},{"text":"Advanced hemodynamic monitoring"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Cardiac OT Technologists benefit from awareness of these technologies, while operation of specialized systems remains the responsibility of appropriately trained professionals."}]},{"heading":"Target Profile at Graduation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A strong Cardiac OT Technologist candidate should ideally demonstrate:"},{"type":"h","text":"Cardiac"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cardiac anatomy"},{"text":"Basic cardiac physiology"},{"text":"Cardiac surgery workflow"},{"text":"Cardiac emergency awareness"}]},{"type":"h","text":"OT"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sterile technique"},{"text":"Instrument preparation"},{"text":"Surgical counts"},{"text":"Patient positioning"},{"text":"OT equipment"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Monitoring"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ECG"},{"text":"SpO₂"},{"text":"BP"},{"text":"Temperature"},{"text":"Invasive monitoring awareness"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Anaesthesia"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Anaesthesia workflow"},{"text":"Airway-equipment awareness"},{"text":"Monitoring setup"},{"text":"Emergency readiness"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Perfusion"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"CPB fundamentals"},{"text":"Perfusion-team workflow"},{"text":"Blood-management awareness"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Digital"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"EMR"},{"text":"OT management systems"},{"text":"Equipment tracking"},{"text":"Excel"}]}]},{"heading":"Recommended Final Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cardiac Anatomy & Physiology"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Cardiac Surgery Workflow"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Operation Theatre Technology"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Surgical Instruments"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Sterile Technique"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Patient Positioning"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Cardiac Monitoring"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Anaesthesia Support"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"CPB / Perfusion Awareness"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Emergency Preparedness"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Infection Control"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Equipment Management"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"EMR / Digital OT Systems"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Clinical Documentation"}]}]},{"heading":"Best Overall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Recognized Cardiac/OT Technology Qualification","Cardiac Surgery Internship","Cardiac OT Technologist","Advanced Cardiac OT Experience","Senior Technologist","Cardiac OT Specialist / Coordinator","OT Management or Clinical Applications"]},{"type":"flow","items":["For maximum employability, combine cardiac surgical workflow","OT technology","sterile technique","cardiac instruments","monitoring","anaesthesia support","perfusion awareness","emergency preparedness","equipment management","digital OT systems."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"note","label":"Career-fitment mapping note","text":"“Cardiac OT Technologist,” “Anaesthesia Technologist,” and “Perfusion Technologist” should remain separate career pathways in the database. They work closely together in cardiac surgery but have different education and technical scopes. A Cardiac OT Technologist supports the cardiac surgical environment; they do not independently perform cardiac surgery, administer anaesthesia, or operate the cardiopulmonary bypass circuit unless separately qualified and authorized for that role."}]}]}